  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef bought a huge (effectively infinite) planar island and built NNN restaurants (numbered 111 through NNN) on it. For each valid iii, the Cartesian coordinates of restaurant iii are (Xi,Yi)(X_i, Y_i)(Xi​,Yi​).\n\nNow, Chef wants to build N−1N-1N−1 straight narrow roads (line segments) on the island. The roads may have arbitrary lengths; restaurants do not have to lie on the roads. The slope of each road must be 111 or −1-1−1, i.e. for any two points (x1,y1)(x_1, y_1)(x1​,y1​) and (x2,y2)(x_2, y_2)(x2​,y2​) on the same road, ∣x1−x2∣=∣y1−y2∣|x_1-x_2| = |y_1-y_2|∣x1​−x2​∣=∣y1​−y2​∣ must hold.\n\nLet's denote the minimum distance Chef has to walk from restaurant iii to reach a road by DiD_iDi​. Then, let's denote a=max (D1,D2,…,DN)a = \\mathrm{max}\\,(D_1, D_2, \\ldots, D_N)a=max(D1​,D2​,…,DN​); Chef wants this distance to be minimum possible.\n\nChef is a busy person, so he decided to give you the job of building the roads. You should find a way to build them that minimises aaa and compute a⋅2a \\cdot \\sqrt{2}a⋅2​.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "2≤N≤1042 \\le N \\le 10^42≤N≤104",
      "∣Xi∣,∣Yi∣≤109|X_i|, |Y_i| \\le 10^9∣Xi​∣,∣Yi​∣≤109 for each valid iii",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (10 points):**",
      "1≤T≤101 \\le T \\le 101≤T≤10",
      "2≤N≤52 \\le N \\le 52≤N≤5",
      "∣Xi∣,∣Yi∣≤10|X_i|, |Y_i| \\le 10∣Xi​∣,∣Yi​∣≤10 for each valid iii",
      "a⋅2a \\cdot \\sqrt{2}a⋅2​ is an integer"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nNNN lines follow. For each valid iii, the iii-th of these lines contains two space-separated integers XiX_iXi​ and YiY_iYi​.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing one real number — the minimum distance aaa multiplied by 2\\sqrt{2}2​. Your answer will be considered correct if its absolute or relative error does not exceed 10−610^{-6}10−6.",
